11. MISSING-VALUE IMPUTATION: SIMPLE PANDAS ALTERNATIVE
---------------------------------------------------------------
Use this for quick data cleaning/EDA when you are not yet evaluating a model.
For machine learning, prefer SimpleImputer inside the Pipeline in Section 10.

# Numeric columns: fill missing values with each column's median
numeric_cols = df.select_dtypes(include=np.number).columns
df[numeric_cols] = df[numeric_cols].fillna(df[numeric_cols].median())

# Categorical/text columns: fill missing values with the most frequent value
categorical_cols = df.select_dtypes(exclude=np.number).columns
for col in categorical_cols:
    if df[col].isnull().any() and not df[col].mode().empty:
        df[col] = df[col].fillna(df[col].mode()[0])

# Check remaining missing values
print(df.isnull().sum())

CAUTION: Do not run this whole-data imputation before train/test splitting for a
final model evaluation. It calculates medians/modes using the whole dataset,
including the test set.

